=3D"position: relative;"><div class=3D"HTMLContent_html__0OZLp" data-qd-ren=
dered-description=3D"" data-track-load=3D"description_content"><p>Given the=
 <code>head</code> of a linked list, remove the <code>n<sup>th</sup></code>=
 node from the end of the list and return its head.</p>

<p>&nbsp;</p>
<p><strong class=3D"example">Example 1:</strong></p>
<img alt=3D"" src=3D"https://assets.leetcode.com/uploads/2020/10/03/remove_=
ex1.jpg" style=3D"width: 542px; height: 222px;">
<pre><strong>Input:</strong> head =3D [1,2,3,4,5], n =3D 2
<strong>Output:</strong> [1,2,3,5]
</pre>

<p><strong class=3D"example">Example 2:</strong></p>

<pre><strong>Input:</strong> head =3D [1], n =3D 1
<strong>Output:</strong> []
</pre>

<p><strong class=3D"example">Example 3:</strong></p>

<pre><strong>Input:</strong> head =3D [1,2], n =3D 1
<strong>Output:</strong> [1]
</pre>

<p>&nbsp;</p>
<p><strong>Constraints:</strong></p>

<ul>
	<li>The number of nodes in the list is <code>sz</code>.</li>
	<li><code>1 &lt;=3D sz &lt;=3D 30</code></li>
	<li><code>0 &lt;=3D Node.val &lt;=3D 100</code></li>
	<li><code>1 &lt;=3D n &lt;=3D sz</code></li>
</ul>

<p>&nbsp;</p>
<p><strong>Follow up:</strong> Could you do this in one pass?</p>
